  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curves $y=x^{3}, y=\\frac{1}{x}, x=2$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$4-\\log _{e} 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}+\\log _{e} 2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$3-\\log _{e} 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{15}{4}-\\log _{e} 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "First of all we draw the graph $y=x^{3}, y=\\frac{1}{x}, x=2$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0019_e3b3b7389825.png\">\r\n\r\nRequired area i.e., (OMPNO) $=\\int_{0}^{1} x^{3} d x+\\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{1}{x} d x$\r\n$=\\left[\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right]_{0}+\\left[\\log _{4} x\\right]_{1}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}+\\log _{c} 2$"
  }
}